INTERVIEW QUESTIONS ON GIT

1)git vs github
Git is a distributed version control system for tracking and managing code changes locally, 
whereas GitHub is a cloud platform that hosts Git repositories and provides collaboration features like pull requests, issue management, and automation.”

2)git pull vr git fetch
git fetch downloads changes from the remote repo without modifying my working copy,allowing me to review them first. 
git pull performs a fetch followed by an automatic merge into my current branch

3)git clone vs git fork
Clone = Downloading a copy of remote repo to local to your computer.
Fork = Making your own copy on GitHub to modify safely.complete copy of someone else’s repository under your GitHub account.

4)git stash
Git stash is used to temporarily save uncommitted changes without committing them, allowing me to switch branches or pull latest changes safely. 
The changes are stored in a stack and can later be restored using git stash apply or git stash pop.

5)git rebase
Git rebase replays commits from one branch on top of another. It’s mainly used to keep a branch updated and maintain a clean, linear history by removing merge commits. 
Rebase rewrites commit history, so it should only be used on local branches that no one else depends on. 

