8)Branching strategy in your project
In our project, we followed a GitFlow-inspired branching strategy.
We had integration for production-ready code and develop for ongoing development.
All new features were developed in feature branches, then merged into develop through Merge Requests with code review and CI validations. 
Before a release, we created a release branch for final QA and UAT. Once approved, it was merged into main and tagged for production.




